Ok, here are two programs and a file.  The programs are "encode"
and "decode".  Encode takes an arbitrary binary file and encodes
all the non-printing characters so that news won't barf on them.
Decode reverses this process.  The file is an encoded picture.
It should be cat'ed to a vt100 compatible terminal for a nifty
surprise.  Be sure to strip off the trailing lines.  Gosh this
turned out to be more work than I expected!

